[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743119620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104398#issuecomment-2743119620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104398","id":2743119620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jgK8E","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T11:41:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T11:41:57Z","body":"We should probably improve documentation on `@tool`.\n\nNon-tool scripts can run in the editor too. A difference between running and non-running script is a ScriptInstance. It's created automatically at runtime, but not created in the editor unless the script is tool. This only applies to attached scripts. By doing `script.new()`, you are creating instance directly and thus the script is able to run in the editor.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743119620/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743271895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104398#issuecomment-2743271895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104398","id":2743271895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jgwHX","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T12:48:48Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T12:48:48Z","body":"KoBeWi's comment is the workaround. Just don't call `new()`, at least not directly.\n\nDo the same as the editor. Create an instance of the base native class and attach the script to it. This avoids creating the script instance and the resource works the same in the inspector.\n\n```gdscript\nvar res = Resource.new()\nres.set_script(NonToolResource)\nnew_array[index] = res\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743271895/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]